#!/bin/bash
# Usage: Tools/test-data [fetch [SET...]|path [SET]|list]
#
# Test and benchmark files that aren't checked in: downloaded from other projects, or made by generator scripts
# that are, into TestData/SET/ at the repository root (ignored by git).
#
#   fetch [SET...]  Download or generate the sets named (default: all). Idempotent: downloaded files already
#                   there with the right SHA-256 are kept, and a generated set is made again only when its
#                   generator's files have changed (or its directory is gone).
#   path [SET]      Print TestData/ (or TestData/SET), the directory tests and benchmarks read.
#   list            Print each set and its files with their sizes (or "missing"), tab-separated.
#
# Downloaded sets (pinned to a revision, checked by SHA-256):
#   swift-binary-parsing  apple/swift-binary-parsing's Sources/TestData/Data (PNG, QOI, ELF, PCAPNG, binary plist
#                         samples), at the revision BinaryParsingComparison's Package.resolved pins. Used by
#                         BinaryParsingComparison's tests and benchmarks.
#   wycheproof            Project Wycheproof's (C2SP/wycheproof) test vectors for AES-GCM, ChaCha20-Poly1305,
#                         HMAC-SHA1/SHA256, HKDF-SHA256/SHA384, ECDSA P-256/SHA-256 and P-384/SHA-384 (DER and
#                         P1363 signatures), ECDH P-256 and P-384, and RSA PKCS #1 v1.5 signatures (2048, 3072,
#                         and 4096 bits with SHA-256/384/512, and the signature-generation sets' 1024–4096-bit
#                         keys with SHA-1 among their hashes): edge cases and known attacks. Used by BytesCrypto's
#                         tests.
#   rfc8448               RFC 8448, "Example Handshake Traces for TLS 1.3": every secret, key, and protected record
#                         of real handshakes. Used by BytesCrypto's TLS tests.
#   rfc9180               RFC 9180's (HPKE) test vectors, from the CFRG draft's repository: every intermediate value
#                         of each mode and suite's key schedule, and its encryptions. Used by BytesCrypto's HPKE tests.
#   c-references          The C codecs BytesCompression's LZFSE, LZVN, and LZBITMAP coders were checked and benchmarked
#                         against while they were written (lzfse at e634ca5, BSD; libzbitmap at 2fcb080, MIT), as
#                         source tarballs. Not built by any package now; Bytes' RESULTS-lz4-lzfse.md and
#                         RESULTS-lzbitmap.md have the comparisons and how to build them again.
#   hpack-test-case       http2jp/hpack-test-case (MIT): real header sets ("stories") encoded by nghttp2, go-hpack,
#                         python-hpack, swift-nio-hpack, and others, with and without Huffman coding, plus the raw
#                         headers. HTTPBytes' HPACK tests and benchmarks.
#   qifs                  qpackers/qifs: QPACK interop files (QIF text of real HTTP/3 traffic) and their encodings by
#                         several QPACK implementations at several table sizes. HTTPBytes' QPACK tests and benchmarks.
#   structured-field-tests  httpwg/structured-field-tests: RFC 9651's test suite (JSON). HTTPBytes' Structured Fields.
#   picohttpparser, llhttp, ls-hpack, ls-qpack
#                         C references for HTTPBytes' benchmarks and differential tests (MIT licensed): h2o's
#                         picohttpparser, llhttp's release v9.4.4 (generated C), LiteSpeed's ls-hpack and ls-qpack
#                         v2.7.1. HTTPBytes/Benchmarks builds them from here.
#   llhttp-tests          llhttp's source tree: its markdown test suite (test/request, test/response), malformed and
#                         smuggling cases for HTTPBytes' HTTP/1 tests.
#   http-garden           narfindustries/http-garden's TROPHIES.md (GPL-3.0, at b417e80): the payload of every parser bug
#                         the HTTP Garden found. Fetched here only, never checked in or copied into the repository.
#   httparse              seanmonstar/httparse's src/lib.rs and tests/uri.rs (MIT/Apache-2.0, at a0fa552): its request
#                         and response tests and 264 request-target cases.
#   http-parser           nodejs/http-parser's test.c (MIT, at ec8b5ee): its request and response messages with the
#                         bodies, keep-alive, and URLs it expects, and its malformed lines.
#   h2o                   h2o/h2o's source tarball (MIT, at d3e43fc), kept packed: h2o-http1-corpus takes its
#                         fuzz/http1-corpus from it.
#   cursed-http           public/cursed-http (MIT): fbparse.h and fbresp.h, SIMD HTTP/1 head parsers (a C reference for
#                         HTTPBytes' benchmarks), and tests/top1k, real requests and responses from the Tranco top 1,000.
# Repository snapshots are `*.unpack.tar.gz` files: unpacked into the set's directory (top directory stripped).
# Generated sets (the generator is run with the output directory as its argument):
#   swift-help-lz4        swift-binary-parsing's ELF/swift-help compressed with `lz4 -9`, for BinaryParsingComparison's
#                         LZ4 and ELF workloads (BinaryParsingComparison/TestDataGenerators; needs Homebrew's lz4).
#   nativezip-formats     Archives from Python's zipfile, Info-ZIP zip, and bsdtar for NativeZip's FormatTests
#                         (NativeZipArchive/Tests/NativeZipTests/Fixtures/formats; needs python3 3.14 or later).
#   nativezip-lzma        LZMA payloads from liblzma for NativeZip's LZMADecoderTests
#                         (NativeZipArchive/Tests/NativeZipTests/Fixtures/lzma; needs Homebrew's xz).
#   nativeaea-synthetic   An Apple Archive laid out like Xcode's (sizes, fields, APFS compression), in a signed `aea`
#                         container with Xcode's settings, for NativeAEA's benchmarks (NativeAEA/Benchmarks/Fixtures).
#   http-corpus           qifs' real traffic as HTTP/1.1 heads and as QIF, one message set for HTTPBytes' HTTP/1, HPACK,
#                         and QPACK rows (HTTPBytes/Fixtures/corpus; needs the qifs set fetched first).
#   llhttp-cases          llhttp's markdown tests as one TSV with llhttp's verdicts, for HTTPBytes' differential HTTP/1 tests
#                         (HTTPBytes/Fixtures/llhttp; needs the llhttp-tests set fetched first).
#   cursed-http-cases     cursed-http's conformance/extract.py (MIT; it gathers other suites' request cases) run over
#                         llhttp-tests, http-garden, picohttpparser, and httparse: one TSV of requests with each suite's
#                         verdict (none for HTTP Garden's payloads)
#                         (HTTPBytes/Fixtures/cursed-http; needs python3 and those five sets fetched first).
#   httparse-cases        httparse's `req!`/`res!` tests and URI tests as one TSV (HTTPBytes/Fixtures/httparse; needs
#                         the httparse set).
#   http-parser-cases     http-parser's messages and `test_simple` lines as one TSV (HTTPBytes/Fixtures/http-parser;
#                         needs the http-parser set).
#   picohttpparser-cases  picohttpparser's test.c requests, responses, header blocks, and chunked bodies as one TSV
